{"_comment": "ORDER-630 (S5). CANONICAL store of Hypothesis rows -- the STRUCTURED, MACHINE-READ fields only (identity, architecture digest, module set, coupling, status). The causal claim, the falsifier and the pre-registered bars stay in the taskboard order and are reached by preregistration_ref; this entity must not restate acceptance criteria. This file carries NO rows yet: registering a hypothesis means asserting a causal claim and pinning the order that pre-registered it, and no such order exists in the B11-B18 form today. Writer: claude|user. No verdict field -- a hypothesis has a STATUS, never a verdict."}
